input.content:
{
  "cr-impact": "cr-requirements and cr-scenarios read impact.md as the pre-change trunk. impact.md lines 57-59 quote spec/invariants.md as it stood on the trunk (\"any entry\"). This change's own convergence edit has since reworded it to \"anything the system stores: any guestbook entry and any to-do task\". No resolution names that section, so I left it as a description of today. For the same reason I left untouched the pre-Q-8 sentence at impact.md line 345 in § What I could not determine (\"`tooling_touched` is recorded absent on that basis\").",
  "cr-requirements": "scenarios.md covers the converged clauses as they stand: S-8 and S-9 (R-2 cl.6), S-33 (R-6 cl.4), S-49 (R-11 cl.6), S-52 and S-53 (R-11 cl.1/5). Its line-break data uses U+000A only, which fits within A-1's seven. No scenario asserts which refusal wins for a text that is both over 200 and multi-line. No scenario covers the new E-21 half-filled case, and it does not need one: it is a recorded exposure, not a requirement.",
  "cr-scenarios": "requirements.md as reconciled is the authority: R-2 clause 6 with R-2.7, R-6 clause 4 with R-6.3, R-11 clauses 1, 5 and 6 with R-11.5, R-11.6 and R-11.7, and A-1 still assumed and waiting for the user. If the user overrules A-1 with U+000A and U+000D only, five of the new rows flip to accepted, and the paragraph says so. The rest of cr-requirements' boundaries are unchanged since pass 1, so the remaining unstated bounds still stand: which refusal wins when a text breaks two rules, the largest number of tasks, and the floor on not-done examples."
}

